  "ingredients": [
    "2 1/4 cup roasted pecans",
    "1/2 cup chia seeds (ground)",
    "1/4 cup erythritol (powdered)",
    "3 large egg",
    "10 drop liquid stevia",
    "3 tablespoon sugar-free salted caramel syrup (such as Torani)",
    "1/4 cup butter (melted)",
    "3 tablespoon heavy whipping cream",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "salt (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350F. Measure out the pecans and spread out on a baking sheet lined with foil. Bake for about 10 minutes. Once nutty and lightly toasted, remove from the oven and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5099.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a spice grinder to grind the chia seeds into a meal.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5104.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the chia meal and place in a bowl. Next, grind the erythritol until powdered, if you aren't using an already powdered form. Use caution when removing the lid. Allowing the powder to settle for a few moments will keep it from coming out in a big pouf. Add it to the same bowl as the chia meal.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5116.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place two-thirds of the roasted pecans in a food processor.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5113.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Process the nuts, scraping down the sides as needed, until a smooth nut butter has formed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5122.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add eggs, liquid stevia, and Torani Salted Caramel syrup to the chia mixture. Mix together well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5124.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the pecan butter to the batter and mix again.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5126.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using a rolling pin, smash the remaining pecans into chunks inside of a plastic bag.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5131.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the crushed pecans and melted butter to the batter and mix well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5132.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the heavy cream, baking powder, and salt to the batter and mix well again.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5142.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour the batter into a baking pan lined with parchment paper, smoothing out the top to make it even.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5147.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20 minutes or until desired consistency is reached. Let cool for about 10 minutes before slicing.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5151.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pecan-butter-chia-seed-blondies/#wprm-recipe-51165-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
